{
  "about": "Three fingers across slide the desktops with them (docs/adr/0046-interactive-gestures.mdx), at 1 (1280 × 720): Allo's two windows on the first desktop, a second added in Mission Control. Left a quarter, half and three quarters of the swipe's 400 pixels hold the first desktop's windows slid that share of the width, in the frame after the motion; lifted slowly past halfway, the second desktop is the active one. Right a quarter brings the first desktop's windows in from the left as far; lifted short it goes back, and a fast short flick goes through, every window exactly where it was. Past the first desktop the windows pull against the end, less and less (half a desktop of the fingers, a tenth of the width), and come back. No application hears anything of it.",
